  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct assistance for displaced and returned communities in North Kivu, Democratic Republic of the CongoDirect assistance for displaced and returned communities in North Kivu, Democratic Republic of the Congo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project aims to address to the urgent needs of populations affected by crises and displacement in the Democratic Republic of Congo, with a particular focus on North Kivu province. Following the escalation of the conflict in 2025, marked by M23 offensives, many displaced and returned persons are enduring precarious living conditions characterized by damaged infrastructure, limited access to clean water and increased vulnerability to disease.  The main objective of the project is to deliver essential humanitarian assistance to improve living conditions and restore dignity among affected populations. To this end, four key outputs are planned: the distribution of essential household items kits, the distribution of menstrual hygiene management (MHM) kits, the construction/rehabilitation of water points, and coordination and accountability.</narrative>
  </description>
